.TH _CYAML_DELETE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
_cyaml_delete \- path-based delete back-end (prefer cyaml_delete macro)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t _cyaml_delete(cyaml root, const char *path);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Navigates to the parent of the node addressed by the dot-separated path
and removes and deep-frees that node.  The path uses the same syntax as
_cyaml_get: plain components address dictionary keys, '#N' components
address list elements by zero-based index, and '\e.' / '\e\e' are escape
sequences for a literal dot or backslash in a key name.

The split is performed on the LAST unescaped dot, so "a.b.c" navigates
to parent "a.b" and removes key "c".  When path has no dot, root itself
is the parent.

Prefer the cyaml_delete() macro for all call sites.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - node removed and freed.
ccol_invalid_args      - root or path is NULL, path is empty, a component
                         is not valid for the node it addresses (e.g. a
                         non-'#N' component on a list, or any component
                         encountered under a scalar), malformed '#N'
                         index syntax, or an empty component (nothing
                         between two dots, or a leading or trailing
                         dot); at any position in the path, not just
                         the leaf.
ccol_key_not_found     - a syntactically well-formed component (a
                         dictionary key or a '#N' index) is absent; at any
                         position, including a syntactically valid but
                         out-of-range list index.
ccol_not_enough_memory - internal strdup failed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_delete (macro) (3),
.BR _cyaml_get (3),
.BR _cyaml_set_typed (3)
